  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "fall asleep and become invincible, summoning companion to buff allied summons and attack enemies",
    "skill1": "summon companion that attacks enemies, detonating for AoE damage on expiry",
    "skill2": "nearby enemies lingering too long are transformed into harmless form",
    "skill3": "ATK scales with variety of allied summons on field",
    "skill4": "while asleep, allied summons enhanced and companion becomes unaffected",
    "skill5": "high energy during sleep expands transformation field radius"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Aurora]] summons a companion that attacks and detonates for area damage, then falls asleep and becomes **invincible** while enhancing allied summons. Nearby enemies who linger can be transformed into harmless forms, and her ATK scales with summon variety on the field. While asleep, allied summons gain stronger effects and the companion becomes Unaffected. She shines beside summon-heavy teams that keep bodies on the field. Few allied summons or a fight that ends before the sleep cycle leave her with little value.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Aurora]] sleeps from battle start and is invincible while dreaming, so never dump burst into that form. Her companion and allied summons do the damage while her sleep state enhances them. Collapse the summon providers with lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] or [[Gwyneth]], then race the line with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]. Do not let a summon-heavy formation build bodies and ATK stacks before the field is cleared."
}
